{"item_id": "mf-boundary-02", "payload_sha256": "de8800eb9f1c6397714d1662fabb9b946cbdcb31729e41e4c51ed6b8f22e1bf5", "transcript_sha256": "42306dfe680e416bb361cc67cd6507396b77801c09d2c2f6f1db96a31d821cfd", "linter_verdict": "clean", "execution_constraint_audit": "clean", "checker_verdict": "PASS", "covariates": {"locality_hops": 3, "files_spanned": 4, "distractor_count": 4, "cue_directness": "none"}, "defect_keys": ["last window", "floor division", "off-by-one", "final window", "generated"], "item_class": "multi_file", "defect_class": "boundary", "size_bytes": 3889, "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "checker_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "attempt": 1, "review_transcript_sha256": "162549ec261f2e702000395f10a664a53cd262f0ab8450d51fbe1dac775232b0", "audit_transcript_sha256": "a4d6a9ec4e10a48dc3077d85d2cb57327037c25d9939e1610fb1bb27094e631c", "blind_review": {"defect_found": true, "defect_class": "boundary", "description": "window_bounds computes the number of windows with floor division (total_span // window_seconds), so the final partial window is dropped and the record at end_time is never included; a span smaller than one window yields zero windows and an empty report. It should round the count up to cover through end_time.", "confidence": "high", "keys_matched": ["floor division"]}, "metadata_audit": {"keys_accurate": true, "covariates_sane": true, "single_defect": true, "notes": ""}}
{"item_id": "mf-comparison-01", "payload_sha256": "344a770a715273a19165756edf899a2b1535446e8482f99a06ac479ae039c83a", "transcript_sha256": "b6c173012ed8c3056f9eb6cd28d4d503e8ca1fb58695296b15b4fcd59dc89e19", "linter_verdict": "clean", "execution_constraint_audit": "clean", "checker_verdict": "PASS", "covariates": {"locality_hops": 1, "files_spanned": 2, "distractor_count": 2, "cue_directness": "indirect"}, "defect_keys": ["recovery timeout", "half open", "circuit breaker"], "item_class": "multi_file", "defect_class": "comparison", "size_bytes": 2970, "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "checker_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "attempt": 2, "review_transcript_sha256": "bbd244d61453cd23127ac7b98952c741c41d4a61e7abc1fba5b6a0cd368f6326", "audit_transcript_sha256": "8be4337aba9574b550d23a6c11ce7b52decfda51abb36b4719127b82fd389eb0", "blind_review": {"defect_found": true, "defect_class": "comparison", "description": "In the circuit breaker's open state, allow_request lets a request through while elapsed <= recovery_timeout and blocks it once the timeout has passed. That's backwards: it should stay open (return False) until the recovery timeout has elapsed, then allow a trial request. As written, it probes immediately after tripping and permanently blocks once the cooldown expires.", "confidence": "high", "keys_matched": ["recovery timeout", "circuit breaker"]}, "metadata_audit": {"keys_accurate": true, "covariates_sane": true, "single_defect": true, "notes": ""}}
{"item_id": "mf-comparison-02", "payload_sha256": "e6e7355d3c766f0d0e41f251c0e73a2ff3a00217fd0b778a4be967e5290b6593", "transcript_sha256": "9df0e6c18a3e050c9b809af66a47adefab12c07d0a395d55841ed0f5e2ac28f8", "linter_verdict": "clean", "execution_constraint_audit": "clean", "checker_verdict": "PASS", "covariates": {"locality_hops": 3, "files_spanned": 4, "distractor_count": 4, "cue_directness": "direct"}, "defect_keys": ["earliest deadline", "latest deadline", "wrong direction", "later deadline", "larger deadline", "prefers the task", "is_more_urgent claims"], "item_class": "multi_file", "defect_class": "comparison", "size_bytes": 4512, "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "checker_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "attempt": 3, "review_transcript_sha256": "1082a5ce28d094ec84d55475b64d909e59ac49b656b39144a73cf8c3a6e79b28", "audit_transcript_sha256": "7afd50e28b38a88003f30c22068ff53df0a0cfc4c0ce6d79126ef1008c72f799", "blind_review": {"defect_found": true, "defect_class": "comparison", "description": "In is_more_urgent, a task due sooner should be more urgent, but it returns True when the candidate's deadline is greater (later) than current_best's. The comparison is inverted, so it schedules the task with the latest deadline first instead of the earliest.", "confidence": "high", "keys_matched": ["latest deadline"]}, "metadata_audit": {"keys_accurate": true, "covariates_sane": true, "single_defect": true, "notes": ""}}
{"item_id": "mf-exception-01", "payload_sha256": "f975e17715f916f05a40adc0f9e8ec02b019b2097c63f5ed23dbc54ded2bce4c", "transcript_sha256": "8bdc3fa60d327cf2e5ab29049dad04040319089b25b39ae1e7749fc1f9c03556", "linter_verdict": "clean", "execution_constraint_audit": "clean", "checker_verdict": "PASS", "covariates": {"locality_hops": 1, "files_spanned": 2, "distractor_count": 0, "cue_directness": "direct"}, "defect_keys": ["too broad", "swallow", "silently", "masks real errors", "catches all exceptions"], "item_class": "multi_file", "defect_class": "exception", "size_bytes": 3250, "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "checker_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "attempt": 1, "review_transcript_sha256": "9ee4421e0cf3e08ab4794e749dbb376c9e23ae353c4d5f37d1726a4c01ac4256", "audit_transcript_sha256": "63a16c7da4c230e6fc843289b2435609110f79c84a023bee79eb6573fdd02294", "blind_review": {"defect_found": true, "defect_class": "exception", "description": "get_rate catches every Exception and returns None, so a ValueError from fetch_live_rate for a malformed or identical currency pair (an invalid lookup) is swallowed and reported as 'no rate available'. The convert docstring explicitly says a pair should be treated as unavailable only when no rate can actually be found, not when the lookup itself was invalid; the broad except conflates the two.", "confidence": "high", "keys_matched": ["swallow"]}, "metadata_audit": {"keys_accurate": true, "covariates_sane": true, "single_defect": true, "notes": ""}}
{"item_id": "mf-exception-02", "payload_sha256": "0b757fe07a5deafaa61cef795d51bfa8ac80c47ec174e50e674f4605b3da528d", "transcript_sha256": "4cf299e835683f30974972945f9a989f07346fac99e8d927541ceb66d8a262bd", "linter_verdict": "clean", "execution_constraint_audit": "clean", "checker_verdict": "PASS", "covariates": {"locality_hops": 3, "files_spanned": 4, "distractor_count": 3, "cue_directness": "indirect"}, "defect_keys": ["silently swallow", "swallowed silently", "fails silently", "silently ignored", "sqlite3.integrityerror"], "item_class": "multi_file", "defect_class": "exception", "size_bytes": 5482, "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "checker_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "attempt": 1, "review_transcript_sha256": "50f5d6e769a48d0f46b7f182cb5097c557ee591eeda7302f222cb584e5b9e82c", "audit_transcript_sha256": "31b0416eedd823a75f14f5b410d7bc3a0bee2f41b022db3005709dd56d6c99e4", "blind_review": {"defect_found": true, "defect_class": "exception", "description": "In store.py, _execute_upsert catches all remaining exceptions with `except Exception: pass`, so any write failure other than OperationalError (e.g. IntegrityError, DataError, or errors building the parameters) is swallowed silently. apply_update then returns as if the delta was applied, and sync.py counts it as applied, so stock updates can be silently lost.", "confidence": "high", "keys_matched": ["swallowed silently"]}, "metadata_audit": {"keys_accurate": true, "covariates_sane": true, "single_defect": true, "notes": ""}}
